{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356998-white-elephant-bonus-artisans","id":1356998,"title":"[White Elephant Bonus!] Artisans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-26T01:05:44-08:00","id":1356998,"title":"[White Elephant Bonus!] Artisans","content":"I was doing some writing for a friend's game, but figured that anyone who doesn't get their White Elephant this year could have this.<br /> <br /> <b>Artisan</b><br /> \u200bThese slender spirits are supremely skilled at woodcraft, but severely introverted. Possessing rough, bark-like skin and lank, unkempt hair, these unassuming elementals can tease wonderful shapes from dead trees with their wooden tools that never seem to wear down or dull.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence </b>2; <b>Willpower</b>4; <b>Join Battle</b> 2 dice<br /> <b>Personal Motes </b>70<br /> <b>Health Levels</b> -0/-1x2/-2x2/-4/Incap.<br /> <b>Actions</b> Read Intentions 5 dice; Senses 5 dice; Shape Wood 10 dice; Social Influence 1 die; Stealth 8 dice; Tracking 6 dice<br /> Appearance 2, Resolve 2, Guile 1<br /> <br /> <b>Combat</b><br /> Attack (Razor Finger Slash) 9 dice (Damage 8)<br /> Combat Movement 5 dice<br /> Evasion 4, Parry 4<br /> Soak/Hardness 4/0 (Ironwood chain shirt +3)<br /> <br /> <i>Merits</i><br /> <br /> <b>Oaken Oracle</b><br /> Artisans often unwittingly reveals the design of things to come when plying their trade; if an artisan makes something for a specific person as a Major or Superior woodworking project, that person may make a difficulty 2 (Perception + Occult) roll. Success informs the character of the next major course their life will take. Artisans are largely unaware that they possess this ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Ironwood Endowment</b><br /> These elementals know the secret of creating ironwood. By spending a Willpower during a Basic or Major woodworking project, an artisan may give the finished item the properties of ironwood.<br /> <br /> <b>Living Wood Taboo</b><br /> Artisans instinctively know not to craft with wood unless it has been dead for at least a month. One will do so if ordered by a summoner, but breaking this taboo renders the spirit's fingers painfully arthritic; the artisan will be unable to craft for an entire year, and loses access to Verdant Palm Caress and Artful Shaper's Hands until then.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Tempered by the Elements (Forest)</b><br /> \u200bArtisans do not treat forested areas as difficult terrain, no matter how densely-packed the vegetation is.<br /> <br /> <i>Crafting Charms</i><br /> <br /> <b>Artful Shaper's Hands</b> (6m; Simple; One task; Essence 2) Working lathe and chisel and hammer, the artisan can complete basic and major woodworking projects with amazing speed; the simplest works can be finished in seconds, while even complex carpentry will not take more than an hour.<br /> <br /> <i>Mobility Charms</i><br /> <br /> <b>Forest Stride</b> (3m, 1i; Supplemental; Instant; Essence 1) The artisan doubles 9s on a movement roll through forest terrain..<br /> <br /> <i>Miscellaneous Charms</i><br /> <br /> <b>Verdant Palm Caress</b> (10m+; Simple; Keywords: Psyche; Instant; Essence 2) The artisan touches a target, which may require a Difficulty 3 gambit in combat, to suffuse him with wood-Essence. Success impassions (Ex3 Core, p. 217) the target's most primal urges for the next day; wild binges, thrill-seeking, and hedonistic sensuality all can be aspects of this behavior. The length of this behavior may be extended by one day per five additional motes spent, to a maximum of three days.<br /> <br /> <b>Woodland Cloak</b> (5m (+1wp); Supplemental; Scene-length; Essence 1) The artisan blends in with a forest environment. The elemental gains 2 non-Charm successes on a Stealth attempt in appropriate terrain. By spending a Willpower, an artisan may physically merge with a tree for a scene, rendering the spirit undetectable by mundane means. Cutting down the tree shunts the artisan into an adjacent space and deals a level of lethal damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-26-2019, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T03:37:11-08:00","id":1357016,"title":"","content":"One slight modification I'd make: Make Forest Stride passive, or at least either reduce the mote cost or give it a longer duration. These are beings of the forest; it makes sense that they can move with ease in it naturally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T04:03:49-08:00","id":1357018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356998-white-elephant-bonus-artisans?p=1357016#post1357016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One slight modification I'd make: Make Forest Stride passive, or at least either reduce the mote cost or give it a longer duration. These are beings of the forest; it makes sense that they can move with ease in it naturally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I moved its ability to treat forest as regular terrain into its own always-on Merit. Is that better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-26-2019, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T05:41:37-08:00","id":1357028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356998-white-elephant-bonus-artisans?p=1357018#post1357018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I moved its ability to treat forest as regular terrain into its own always-on Merit. Is that better?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good to me. I like the fact that their crafting Charm doesn't obviate the need for tools, 'cause that means they're encouraged to make arrays of ironwood tools - and, for that matter, to give new Artisans their own sets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T05:51:53-08:00","id":1357032,"title":"","content":"Oh, I would reduce the cost of Forest Stride a little - it's only 9-again under limited circumstances, which seems more 3m, 1i, at most, to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T06:02:44-08:00","id":1357035,"title":"","content":"Granted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356998-white-elephant-bonus-artisans?p=1357028#post1357028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds good to me. I like the fact that their crafting Charm doesn't obviate the need for tools, 'cause that means they're encouraged to make arrays of ironwood tools - and, for that matter, to give new Artisans their own sets.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also means that an artisan might have its own future encoded in its tools, all without ever realizing it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}